Let me recall RFC6962 formats exactly.

RFC6962 LogEntry structure (section 3.1):
```
   enum { x509_entry(0), precert_entry(1), (255) } LogEntryType;

   struct {
       LogEntryType entry_type;
       select (entry_type) {
           case x509_entry: ASN.1Cert;
           case precert_entry: PreCert;
       } entry;
   } LogEntry;

   struct {
       opaque issuer_key_hash[32];
       TBSCertificate tbs_certificate;
   } PreCert;

   opaque ASN.1Cert<1..2^24-1>;
```

The "MerkleTreeLeaf" structure (section 3.4):
```
   enum { timestamped_entry(0), (255) } MerkleLeafType;

   struct {
       uint8 version;
       MerkleLeafType leaf_type;
       select (leaf_type) {
           case timestamped_entry: TimestampedEntry;
       }
   } MerkleTreeLeaf;

   struct {
       uint64 timestamp;
       LogEntryType entry_type;
       select (entry_type) {
           case x509_entry: ASN.1Cert;
           case precert_entry: PreCert;
       } signed_entry;
       CtExtensions extensions;
   } TimestampedEntry;

   opaque CtExtensions<0..2^16-1>;
```

The leaf hash is `SHA256(0x00 || MerkleTreeLeaf)`.

So:
- `MerkleTreeLeaf` = version(1 byte = 0) || leaf_type(1 byte = 0 for timestamped_entry) || TimestampedEntry.
- TimestampedEntry = timestamp (8 bytes big-endian) || entry_type (1 byte: 0=x509, 1=precert) || signed_entry (x509: thus entries with data as opaque; precert: issuer_key_hash(32) + tbs_certificate) || extensions (2-byte length prefix + extension data).
- The index is embedded in the extensions field.

So the ctonly.Entry needs fields:
- RawCert/CertData
- timestamp
- isPrecert
- issuerKeyHash (for precerts)
- tbsCertificate (for precerts)
- and we embed the index in the CtExtensions.

